  "method": "One staged data owner and fixed 512 KiB reads in both arms. Flat polls up to 24 events, clips to a 128-event callback budget and services fresh first inside each set. Nested uses the existing second kqueue: poll up to 128 interactive events, then up to 12 bulk events, repolling the interactive queue between batches. Its 128-event callback guard is checked between batches; these samples require 33 data/marker events at most. Unlike a normal standalone accept owner, data_workers=2 in both arms. This is the combined effect of the actual queue topology, classification/migration and drain policies. Sixteen bulk streams. Each array index is the arrival position from zero through the 16th bulk write; zero queues the marker after existing bulk but before the first poll. All bytes and both FINs verified at every position. Each topology ran twice in ABBA order. The four additional sanitizer cases revoke pressured leases and check end-to-end bytes; no service, VM, IP socket or shared worker was used."
